# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots Dovecot (unpatchable 2.3.x, pre-auth overflow) on
# 0.0.0.0:143 / :993 then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the vulnerable service is ALREADY LISTENING on all interfaces when the
#     agent starts (a do-nothing agent must fail the firewall check);
#   * PID 1 is `sleep infinity`, so reloading/restarting dovecot cannot kill it.
#
# The primary LIVE compensating control is the iptables restriction on 143/993
# (read from the running kernel table). Requiring TLS (ssl = required) and
# login_trusted_networks are config-hardening asserted via `doveconf`, which
# also validates the config is parseable — an invalid edit makes dovecot fail to
# stay up and the liveness regression fails.
